  "id": "COMPOUND:20184 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "Asparacoside is implicated in the target pathway leading to Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of molecular interactions involving hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that Asparacoside acts on hepatocytes, which in turn are targeted by multiple related compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one, all of which share a common target of Carboxylesterase 2. This indicates that Asparacoside may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of Carboxylesterase 2 in hepatocytes. The consistent involvement of hepatocytes as a target and the shared target of Carboxylesterase 2 across different compounds suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of enzyme activity in liver cells. The evidence supports a role for Asparacoside in influencing Carboxylesterase 2 through a pathway that involves hepatocytes, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
